# K1f silent-freeze forensics for munch.
#
# Merge after munch-mm-diag.config, k1a, k1b and k1c (the K1e trace chain):
#   make O=out vendor/munch_defconfig munch-mm-diag.config \
#        munch-mm-diag-k1a.config munch-mm-diag-k1b.config \
#        munch-mm-diag-k1c.config munch-mm-diag-k1f.config
#
# 2026-07-24 ~07:30: the phone froze totally on K1e — no panic, no watchdog
# bite, and pstore was empty after the forced cold reset. K1e has no lockup
# or hung-task detection compiled in, and QCOM_WATCHDOG_V2's pet task
# evidently kept running (consistent with a reclaim livelock rather than an
# all-core hard lockup). K1f adds the minimal blocked-task/soft-lockup
# detectors so a recurrence panics into ramoops and warm-reboots instead of
# freezing silently forever. Panic-on-detection is compiled in because a
# silent freeze can make userspace unavailable before a boot script can act.
#
# DEBUG_KERNEL was in the K1-era bootloop suspect set but was never isolated
# (it was removed together with debugfs and page-owner). K1f re-enables ONLY
# DEBUG_KERNEL plus the two detectors; everything else from that suspect set
# stays off, so a RAM-only boot test of this image doubles as the isolation
# experiment.

CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y
CONFIG_DETECT_HUNG_TASK=y
CONFIG_DEFAULT_HUNG_TASK_TIMEOUT=120
CONFIG_SOFTLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_HUNG_TASK_PANIC=y
CONFIG_BOOTPARAM_SOFTLOCKUP_PANIC=y
# CONFIG_HARDLOCKUP_DETECTOR is not set

# SCHED_DEBUG defaults on under DEBUG_KERNEL but kernel/sched/debug.c does
# not compile against this tree's scheduler backport; keep it off.
# CONFIG_SCHED_DEBUG is not set

# Do not enable unrelated debug overhead just because DEBUG_KERNEL is the
# dependency gate for the two detectors.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_PREEMPT is not set
# CONFIG_RCU_TRACE is not set

# Keep the still-unisolated K1 bootloop suspects off.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is not set
# CONFIG_PAGE_EXTENSION is not set
# CONFIG_PAGE_OWNER is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_LIST is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_VM is not set
